{"schemaVersion":2,"book":"PRO","chapter":18,"sourceModule":"original-languages-step","targetBible":"bsb","proposalMethod":"exact STEPBible English gloss match against fixed BSB text","targetTexts":{"1":"He who isolates himself pursues selfish desires; he rebels against all sound judgment.","2":"A fool does not delight in understanding, but only in airing his opinions.","3":"With a wicked man comes contempt as well, and shame is accompanied by disgrace.","4":"The words of a man’s mouth are deep waters; the fountain of wisdom is a bubbling brook.","5":"Showing partiality to the wicked is not good, nor is depriving the innocent of justice.","6":"A fool’s lips bring him strife, and his mouth invites a beating.","7":"A fool’s mouth is his ruin, and his lips are a snare to his soul.","8":"The words of a gossip are like choice morsels that go down into the inmost being.","9":"Whoever is slothful in his work is brother to him who destroys.","10":"The name of the LORD is a strong tower; the righteous run to it and are safe.","11":"A rich man’s wealth is his fortified city; it is like a high wall in his imagination.","12":"Before his downfall a man’s heart is proud, but humility comes before honor.","13":"He who answers a matter before he hears it—this is folly and disgrace to him.","14":"The spirit of a man can endure his sickness, but who can survive a broken spirit?","15":"The heart of the discerning acquires knowledge, and the ear of the wise seeks it out.","16":"A man’s gift opens doors for him, and brings him before great men.","17":"The first to state his case seems right until another comes and cross-examines him.","18":"Casting the lot ends quarrels and separates strong opponents.","19":"An offended brother is harder to win than a fortified city, and disputes are like the bars of a castle.","20":"From the fruit of his mouth a man’s belly is filled; with the harvest from his lips he is satisfied.","21":"Life and death are in the power of the tongue, and those who love it will eat its fruit.","22":"He who finds a wife finds a good thing and obtains favor from the LORD.","23":"The poor man pleads for mercy, but the rich man answers harshly.","24":"A man of many companions may come to ruin, but there is a friend who stays closer than a brother."},"targetSegments":{"1":[{"id":"PRO.18.1.s1","position":1,"text":"He","normalized":"he"},{"id":"PRO.18.1.s2","position":2,"text":"who","normalized":"who"},{"id":"PRO.18.1.s3","position":3,"text":"isolates","normalized":"isolates"},{"id":"PRO.18.1.s4","position":4,"text":"himself","normalized":"himself"},{"id":"PRO.18.1.s5","position":5,"text":"pursues","normalized":"pursues"},{"id":"PRO.18.1.s6","position":6,"text":"selfish","normalized":"selfish"},{"id":"PRO.18.1.s7","position":7,"text":"desires","normalized":"desires"},{"id":"PRO.18.1.s8","position":8,"text":"he","normalized":"he"},{"id":"PRO.18.1.s9","position":9,"text":"rebels","normalized":"rebels"},{"id":"PRO.18.1.s10","position":10,"text":"against","normalized":"against"},{"id":"PRO.18.1.s11","position":11,"text":"all","normalized":"all"},{"id":"PRO.18.1.s12","position":12,"text":"sound","normalized":"sound"},{"id":"PRO.18.1.s13","position":13,"text":"judgment","normalized":"judgment"}],"2":[{"id":"PRO.18.2.s1","position":1,"text":"A","normalized":"a"},{"id":"PRO.18.2.s2","position":2,"text":"fool","normalized":"fool"},{"id":"PRO.18.2.s3","position":3,"text":"does","normalized":"does"},{"id":"PRO.18.2.s4","position":4,"text":"not","normalized":"not"},{"id":"PRO.18.2.s5","position":5,"text":"delight","normalized":"delight"},{"id":"PRO.18.2.s6","position":6,"text":"in","normalized":"in"},{"id":"PRO.18.2.s7","position":7,"text":"understanding","normalized":"understanding"},{"id":"PRO.18.2.s8","position":8,"text":"but","normalized":"but"},{"id":"PRO.18.2.s9","position":9,"text":"only","normalized":"only"},{"id":"PRO.18.2.s10","position":10,"text":"in","normalized":"in"},{"id":"PRO.18.2.s11","position":11,"text":"airing","normalized":"air